From 878ecba982cbae5bef43c759dcef15d46e3b1e97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:43:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] lib: sbi: emulate F and D arithmetic for harts that trap on
 it

For a hart that has the f registers, their loads, stores, moves and
compares but raises an illegal instruction on the arithmetic, square
root, fused multiply-add, min/max and conversions (the Kakao SOC's
kakao64): sbi_fp_emu.c does them with Berkeley SoftFloat 3e
(lib/sbi/softfloat, its RISC-V specialization).
